-- title:
--   Rational j of the quotient by a Γ₀(M')-kernel
-- statement:
--   Fix a commutative ring $A$, natural numbers $\ell$, $M'$, $q$ with $M' \neq 0$, and two variable-change compatibilities: $h\ell$, asserting that for every $A$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, every variable change $C$ and every quadruple $D = (x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$ of elements of $T$, if $D$ is a level-$\ell$ structure on $W$ (both points satisfy the affine equation, both $x$-coordinates are roots of $W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell$, and both independence elements $\mathrm{indepElt}$ are units) then $D.\mathrm{variableChange}\ C$ is one on $C \bullet W$; and $hM$, asserting the analogous statement for the predicate `IsGamma0PowAt` at $(p,k)$, with the kernel polynomial $h$ transported by `kernelVariableChangeDeg`. Fix moreover relative group laws $\mathcal G$ on projective Weierstrass models with unit discriminant and a level transport $\mathcal T$ for $\mathcal G$ at $q$. Let $\mathbb K$ be a field of characteristic zero which is an $A$-algebra and let $x$ be a raw datum over $\mathbb K$ for the rigidified problem `rigidDataPow A ℓ M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯` (so $x.\mathrm{curve}$ is a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb K$ with unit discriminant, carrying level data $x.\mathrm{level}$ consisting of the $\Gamma_0$-power part, a level-$\ell$ part and a Drinfeld part, satisfying the corresponding level predicates). Assume $c_4^3/\Delta$ of $x.\mathrm{curve}$ is transcendental over $\mathbb Q$. Let $\Omega$ be an algebraically closed field that is an algebraic extension of $\mathbb K$, and let $d$ be a nonzero divisor of $M'$. Then there is a single $J \in \mathbb K$ such that for every point $g$ of the affine curve $x.\mathrm{curve}$ base changed to $\Omega$ which is cut out by the $\Gamma_0$-data of $x$ — meaning $g$ has additive order exactly $M'$, and for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, every $n \in \mathbb N$ and every nonsingular affine point $(x_1,y_1)$ over $\Omega$ with $n \cdot g = (x_1,y_1)$ and $\mathrm{addOrderOf}(n \cdot g) = p^{v_p(M')}$, the element $x_1$ is a root of the image in $\Omega[X]$ of the polynomial $x.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$ — the image of $J$ in $\Omega$ equals $(x.\mathrm{curve}$ base changed to $\Omega)$'s `cyclicQuotientJ` at the subgroup generated by $(M'/d) \cdot g$ with parameter $d$, that is $c_4^3/\Delta$ of the quotient of the curve by that subgroup of order $d$.
--
--   This supplies, for a raw Weierstrass datum with $\Gamma_0(M')$-, level-$\ell$- and Drinfeld-level structure over a field of characteristic zero with transcendental $j$-invariant, a single element of the base field representing the $j$-invariant of the quotient by the order-$d$ part of the cyclic subgroup cut out by the $\Gamma_0$-data; the point of the formulation is that the value is independent of the chosen generator $g$ and already rational over $\mathbb K$. It is used in the classification of $\Gamma_0(M')$-data on Tate curves via $q$-expansions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_DrinfeldGlobal_exists_algebraMap_eq_cyclicQuotientJ_of_raw_rigidDataPow.lean

